ENTRY 11757 {"id":11757,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"packages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:89:        { name: \"workspace-pi-conv-20\", createdAt: ago(60) },\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:90:        { name: \"workspace-pi-conv-99\", createdAt: ago(60) },\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:106:        { name: \"workspace-pi-conv-99\", createdAt: ago(60) },\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:107:        { name: \"workspace-pi-conv-20\", createdAt: ago(60) },\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:108:        { name: \"workspace-pi-conv-10\", createdAt: ago(60) },\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:120:        { name: \"workspace-e2e-phase1\", createdAt: ago(600) },\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:121:        { name: \"workspace-pi-conv-99\", createdAt: ago(1) },\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:206:      pvcs: [{ name: \"workspace-pi-conv-99\", createdAt: ago(60) }],\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweeper.test.ts:19:    listPvcs: () => Promise.resolve([{ name: \"workspace-pi-conv-9\", createdAt: OLD }]),\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts:11: *  - a PVC `workspace-pi-conv-<n>` for which no SandboxClaim of that name exists;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts:75:const PVC_NAME = /^workspace-(pi-conv-(\\d+))$/;\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:243:    // `workspace-cloned` once per session; `workspace-present` after a restart. tests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh greps both.\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:244:    log(outcome === \"cloned\" ? \"workspace-cloned\" : \"workspace-present\", {\npackages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts:139:  // The Sandbox controller names the PVC after the volume claim template and the Sandbox (`workspace-<claim>`).\npackages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts:140:  const pvc = { name: `workspace-${claimName}`, namespace };\ntests/e2e/run-phase1.sh:67:k wait --for=delete \"pvc/workspace-$claim\" --timeout=120s >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\ntests/e2e/run-phase3.sh:308:  pvc0=$(k get pvc \"workspace-$claim\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}')\ntests/e2e/run-phase3.sh:314:  pvc1=$(k get pvc \"workspace-$claim\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}')\ntests/e2e/run-phase3.sh:316:  assert \"it mounts the same PVC claim name\" test \"$(k get pod \"$claim\" -o jsonpath='{.spec.volumes[?(@.name==\"workspace\")].persistentVolumeClaim.claimName}')\" = \"workspace-$claim\"\ntests/e2e/run-phase3.sh:350:  assert \"separate PVCs\" test \"$(k get pvc \"workspace-$ca\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}')\" != \"$(k get pvc \"workspace-$cb\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}')\"\ntests/e2e/run-phase4.sh:78:        k delete pvc \"workspace-$claim\" --ignore-not-found --wait=false >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\ntests/e2e/run-phase4.sh:183:pvc_exists() { k get pvc \"workspace-$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1; }\ntests/e2e/run-phase4.sh:189:pvc_uid() { k get pvc \"workspace-$1\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}'; }\ntests/e2e/run-phase4.sh:489:  pvc=workspace-$claim\ntests/e2e/run-phase4.sh:527:  assert \"separate PVCs\" test \"$(k get pvc \"workspace-$ca\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}')\" != \"$(k get pvc \"workspace-$cb\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}')\"\ntests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh:11:#   restart-skip  after an orchestrator restart the clone is found and skipped (log `workspace-present`, no\ntests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh:12:#                 `workspace-cloned`), and a file the agent wrote in the clone is still there\ntests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh:188:  assert_eq \"the orchestrator logged one clone\" 1 \"$(orch_log | grep -c \"\\\"event\\\":\\\"workspace-cloned\\\".*$id\")\"\ntests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh:222:  assert_eq \"the clone was found and skipped\" 1 \"$(orch_log | grep -c \"\\\"event\\\":\\\"workspace-present\\\".*$repo_session\")\"\ntests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh:223:  assert_eq \"no second clone after the restart\" 0 \"$(orch_log | grep -c \"\\\"event\\\":\\\"workspace-cloned\\\".*$repo_session\" || true)\"\n     1\t// Cluster-only, driven in phases by tests/e2e/run-phase1.sh (PI_SANDBOX_E2E=1 plus the bridge env\n     2\t// contract, see src/config.ts). Each phase is a separate process, because the point is that a fresh\n     3\t// runner reattaches to the claim by name:\n     4\t//   PI_E2E_PHASE=write  write a marker file through the env, then exit\n     5\t//   PI_E2E_PHASE=read   (fresh runner) read the marker back\n     6\t//   PI_E2E_PHASE=after-pod-loss  (Pod was deleted and recreated) probe until the env works, read the marker\n     7\t// PI_E2E_RUN_ID names the marker so reruns never see each other's files.\n     8\timport { resolve } from \"node:path\";\n     9\timport { BACKGROUND_CONTEXT } from \"@earendil-works/chord/context\";\n    10\timport { afterAll, describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\n    11\timport { connectSandboxEnv } from \"../src/index.ts\";\n    12\t\n    13\tconst enabled = process.env.PI_SANDBOX_E2E === \"1\";\n    14\tconst phase = process.env.PI_E2E_PHASE ?? \"\";\n    15\tconst runId = process.env.PI_E2E_RUN_ID ?? \"manual\";\n    16\tconst marker = `/workspace/e2e-reattach-${runId}.txt`;\n    17\tconst content = `reattach-marker ${runId}\\n`;\n    18\t\n    19\tdescribe.skipIf(!enabled)(\"sandbox-env reattach\", () => {\n    20\t  const sandbox = connectSandboxEnv({\n    21\t    claimName: process.env.PI_SANDBOX_CLAIM ?? \"\",\n    22\t    namespace: process.env.PI_SANDBOX_NAMESPACE ?? \"\",\n    23\t    cwd: \"/workspace\",\n    24\t    id: \"pi-env:reattach\",\n    25\t    bridgeCommand: [process.execPath, resolve(import.meta.dirname, \"../dist/cli.js\")],\n    26\t  });\n    27\t  afterAll(() => sandbox.close());\n    28\t\n    29\t  it.runIf(phase === \"write\")(\"writes a file through the env\", async () => {\n    30\t    const written = await sandbox.env.writeFile(marker, content, BACKGROUND_CONTEXT);\n    31\t    expect(written.ok).toBe(true);\n    32\t  });\n    33\t\n    34\t  it.runIf(phase === \"read\")(\"reads the file back from a fresh runner\", async () => {\n    35\t    const read = await sandbox.env.readTextFile(marker, BACKGROUND_CONTEXT);\n    36\t    expect(read).toEqual({ ok: true, value: content });\n    37\t  });\n    38\t\n    39\t  // Timeout covers the worst case DNS staleness plus a cold bridge start on every attempt.\n    40\t  it.runIf(phase === \"after-pod-loss\")(\n    41\t    \"works again after the Pod was recreated, with the PVC intact\",\n    42\t    async () => {\n    43\t      const started = performance.now();\n    44\t      const log: string[] = [];\n    45\t      let readBack: string | undefined;\n    46\t      for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= 40 && readBack === undefined; attempt++) {\n    47\t        const t0 = performance.now();\n    48\t        const read = await sandbox.env.readTextFile(marker, BACKGROUND_CONTEXT);\n    49\t        const ms = Math.round(performance.now() - t0);\n    50\t        const at = Math.round((performance.now() - started) / 100) / 10;\n    51\t        if (read.ok) readBack = read.value;\n    52\t        log.push(\n    53\t          `attempt ${String(attempt)} at +${String(at)}s took ${String(ms)}ms: ${read.ok ? \"ok\" : String(read.error)}`,\n    54\t        );\n    55\t        if (!read.ok) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 1000));\n    56\t      }\n    57\t      // The observation phase1 asks for: did the first call fail, how long until it worked.\n    58\t      console.log(`DNS-STALENESS ${log.join(\" | \")}`);\n    59\t      expect(readBack).toBe(content);\n    60\t    },\n    61\t    180_000,\n    62\t  );\n    63\t});\n     4\t// from src/config.ts set: node --experimental-strip-types test/stdio-smoke.e2e.ts\n     5\timport { createHash, randomBytes } from \"node:crypto\";\n     6\timport { sandboxStart } from \"../src/sandbox-client.ts\";\n     7\t\n     8\tconst MIB = 1024 * 1024;\n     9\tconst TOTAL = 64 * MIB;\n    10\tconst authToken = process.env.PI_SANDBOX_AUTH_TOKEN;\n    11\t\n    12\tconst received = createHash(\"sha256\");\n    13\tlet receivedBytes = 0;\n    14\tconst proc = await sandboxStart({\n    15\t  claimName: process.env.PI_SANDBOX_CLAIM ?? \"\",\n    16\t  namespace: process.env.PI_SANDBOX_NAMESPACE ?? \"\",\n    17\t  connectivity: \"in-cluster-service\",\n    18\t  ...(authToken ? { authToken } : {}),\n    19\t})(\"cat\", [], {\n    20\t  onStdout: (chunk) => {\n    21\t    received.update(chunk);\n    22\t    receivedBytes += chunk.length;\n    23\t  },\n    24\t  onStderr: () => undefined,\n    25\t});\n    26\t\n    27\tconst sent = createHash(\"sha256\");\n    28\tconst began = performance.now();\n    29\tfor (let offset = 0; offset < TOTAL; offset += MIB) {\n    30\t  const chunk = randomBytes(MIB);\n    31\t  sent.update(chunk);\n    32\t  await proc.write(chunk);\n    33\t}\n    34\tawait proc.closeStdin();\n    35\tconst { exitCode } = await proc.wait();\n    36\tconst seconds = (performance.now() - began) / 1000;\n    37\tawait proc.close();\n    38\t\n    39\tconst sentHex = sent.digest(\"hex\");\n    40\tconst receivedHex = received.digest(\"hex\");\n    41\tconst ok = exitCode === 0 && receivedBytes === TOTAL && sentHex === receivedHex;\n    42\tconsole.log(\n    43\t  `smoke: ${ok ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\"} exit=${String(exitCode)} bytes=${String(receivedBytes)}/${String(TOTAL)} ` +\n    44\t    `sha256 ${sentHex === receivedHex ? \"match\" : `mismatch ${sentHex} vs ${receivedHex}`} ` +\n    45\t    `time=${seconds.toFixed(2)}s round-trip=${(TOTAL / MIB / seconds).toFixed(1)} MiB/s ` +\n    46\t    `(each direction)`,\n    47\t);\n    48\tprocess.exit(ok ? 0 : 1);\nrun_id=$(date +%s)-$$\nwork=$(mktemp -d)\nk() { kubectl ${ctx:+--context=\"$ctx\"} -n \"$ns\" \"$@\"; }\nlog() { printf '\\n== %s\\n' \"$*\"; }\nfail() { printf 'FAIL: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\n\ncleanup() {\n  rm -rf \"$work\"\n  if [[ -z \"${KEEP_RUNNER:-}\" ]]; then\n    k delete pod e2e-runner --ignore-not-found --wait=false >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n  fi\n  # The claim is this run's own; its workspace PVC (owned by the Sandbox) goes with it.\n  k delete sandboxclaim \"$claim\" --ignore-not-found --wait=false >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT\n\n[[ -s $bundle ]] || fail \"no bundle at $bundle: run tests/e2e/run.sh phase1\"\n\n# Fresh runner pod with the code unpacked at /work/app. Called again to model an orchestrator restart.\nstart_runner() {\n  k delete pod e2e-runner --ignore-not-found --wait=true >/dev/null\n  k create -f \"$here/runner-pod.yaml\" >/dev/null\n  k wait --for=condition=Ready pod/e2e-runner --timeout=240s >/dev/null\n  k exec -i e2e-runner -- sh -c 'mkdir -p /work/app && tar xzf - -C /work/app' <\"$bundle\"\n}\n\n# The claim's token, derived inside the runner by the bundle's own deriveSandboxToken from the master in its env.\nderive_js='import {deriveSandboxToken as d} from \"/work/app/dist/index.js\"; process.stdout.write(d(process.env.PI_SANDBOX_MASTER_KEY, process.env.PI_SANDBOX_CLAIM))'\n# Runs a command in the runner from the app dir with the e2e switches set.\nin_runner() { k exec e2e-runner -- bash -c \"set -o pipefail; export NO_COLOR=1 PI_SANDBOX_E2E=1 PI_E2E_RUN_ID=$run_id PI_SANDBOX_CLAIM=$claim; export PI_SANDBOX_AUTH_TOKEN=\\$(node --input-type=module -e '$derive_js'); cd /work/app; $*\"; }\nvitest_phase() { in_runner \"PI_E2E_PHASE=$1 ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run test/reattach.e2e.test.ts --reporter=verbose\"; }\n\npod_uid() { k get pod \"$claim\" -o jsonpath='{.metadata.uid}' 2>/dev/null || true; }\n\nlog \"start runner\"\nstart_runner\n\nlog \"create claim $claim with the hash of its own token\"\nhash_js='import {deriveSandboxToken as d, sandboxTokenSha256 as h} from \"/work/app/dist/index.js\"; process.stdout.write(h(d(process.env.PI_SANDBOX_MASTER_KEY, process.env.PI_SANDBOX_CLAIM)))'\ntoken_sha=$(k exec e2e-runner -- env PI_SANDBOX_CLAIM=\"$claim\" node --input-type=module -e \"$hash_js\")\n[[ $token_sha =~ ^[0-9a-f]{64}$ ]] || fail \"could not derive the token hash for $claim (is the master in secret sandboxd-auth?)\"\nk delete sandboxclaim \"$claim\" --ignore-not-found --wait=true >/dev/null\nk wait --for=delete \"pvc/workspace-$claim\" --timeout=120s >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\nk create -f - >/dev/null <<YAML\napiVersion: extensions.agents.x-k8s.io/v1beta1\nkind: SandboxClaim\nmetadata:\n  name: $claim\nspec:\n  warmPoolRef: { name: pi-env-pool }\n  env:\n    - { name: SANDBOXD_AUTH_TOKEN_SHA256, value: \"$token_sha\" }\nYAML\nfor _ in $(seq 1 120); do k get \"pod/$claim\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && break; sleep 1; done\nk wait --for=condition=Ready \"pod/$claim\" --timeout=300s >/dev/null || fail \"sandbox pod $claim not Ready\"\n\nlog \"stdio smoke\"\nin_runner \"node --experimental-strip-types test/stdio-smoke.e2e.ts 2>&1 | grep -v agentic-sandbox-client | tee /work/smoke.log; grep -q 'smoke: PASS' /work/smoke.log\" \\\n  || fail \"stdio smoke\"\n\nlog \"env conformance\"\nin_runner \"./node_modules/.bin/vitest run test/conformance.e2e.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -15\" \\\n  | tee \"$work/conformance.log\" || fail \"conformance\"\ngrep -Eq 'Tests +[0-9]+ passed' \"$work/conformance.log\" || fail \"conformance: no passing summary\"\n\nlog \"reattach (a): write, kill runner pod, fresh runner reads\"\nvitest_phase write || fail \"reattach write\"\nstart_runner   # deletes the old pod first: the old orchestrator is gone\nvitest_phase read || fail \"reattach read from fresh runner\"\n\nlog \"reattach (b): delete the sandbox Pod, wait for recreation, same PVC\"\nold_uid=$(pod_uid)\nk delete pod \"$claim\" --wait=true >/dev/null\nfor _ in $(seq 1 120); do\n  new_uid=$(pod_uid)\n  [[ -n \"$new_uid\" && \"$new_uid\" != \"$old_uid\" ]] && break\n  sleep 1\ndone\n[[ -n \"${new_uid:-}\" && \"$new_uid\" != \"$old_uid\" ]] || fail \"sandbox Pod was not recreated\"\nk wait --for=condition=Ready \"pod/$claim\" --timeout=240s >/dev/null || fail \"recreated Pod not Ready\"\necho \"pod recreated and Ready: $old_uid -> $new_uid\"\nvitest_phase after-pod-loss 2>&1 | tee \"$work/after.log\" || fail \"env after Pod recreation\"\ngrep 'DNS-STALENESS' \"$work/after.log\" || true\n\nlog \"ALL PHASE 1 E2E CHECKS PASSED\"\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11820 {"id":11820,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]## Findings\n\n### 1. Cleanup can delete a claim this run never created\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: tests/e2e/run-phase1.sh:37\n- What happens: If the bundle is missing or runner startup fails, the EXIT trap still deletes the claim named by `CLAIM`, including any pre-existing workspace associated with it. This can happen before the script reaches its explicit claim deletion or creation.\n- Evidence: `k delete sandboxclaim \"$claim\" --ignore-not-found --wait=false`\n- Fix idea: Use a unique claim name per run and track whether this run created it. Only delete a claim that the run owns.\n\n### 2. The PVC deletion wait can fail immediately and is ignored\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: tests/e2e/run-phase1.sh:67\n- What happens: When a previous workspace PVC still exists, `kubectl wait` needs to watch it, but the driver Role lacks the PVC `watch` permission. The suppressed failure lets the script create the replacement claim before the old PVC is gone, potentially reusing a stale workspace or racing its deletion.\n- Evidence: `k wait --for=delete \"pvc/workspace-$claim\" --timeout=120s >/dev/null 2>&1 || true`\n- Fix idea: Grant the driver PVC watch permission and treat an unsuccessful wait as an error before creating the claim.\n\n### 3. The namespace override does not apply to the runner manifest\n- Severity: low\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: tests/e2e/run-phase1.sh:46\n- What happens: Setting `NAMESPACE` to anything other than `pi-durable-poc` causes runner creation to fail because `runner-pod.yaml` explicitly specifies `pi-durable-poc`, conflicting with the namespace passed to kubectl.\n- Evidence: `k create -f \"$here/runner-pod.yaml\"`; the manifest sets `namespace: pi-durable-poc`.\n- Fix idea: Remove the hard-coded namespace from the runner manifest or render it using the selected namespace.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
